            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "খাওয়ার পরে আমি এঁটো থালাগুলো বেসিনে রাখলাম। Khāoyār pôre āmi ẽṭo thālāgulo besine rākhlām. After the meal I put the used plates in the basin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "এঁটো (ẽṭo) comes from a reconstructed ācaṣṭa, \"tasted\"; CDIAL lists Bengali ẽṭo, \"the leavings of a meal\" (CDIAL 1067). Food, or a plate, that someone has already eaten from is এঁটো."
            }
