        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: আঁচানো",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আঁচানো — ā̃chāno — \"to rinse after a meal (the mouth and hands)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "খাওয়ার পরে সবাই উঠে আঁচাল। Khāoyār pôre sôbāi uṭhe ā̃chālô. After the meal everyone got up and rinsed their mouths and hands."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি খাওয়ার পরে আঁচালেন, tini khāoyār pôre ā̃chālen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Rice is often eaten by hand, so mouth and hand are rinsed when the meal is over."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "আঁচানো (ā̃chāno) comes down from Sanskrit ācāmati, taking a sip of water from the hollow of the hand (CDIAL 1069, which lists Bengali ā̃cāna). The everyday sense, rinsing mouth and hand at the end of a meal, probably grew out of that sip."
            }
          ]
        },
